-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/(SICI)1521-3757(19990301)111:5<746::AID-ANGE746>3.0.CO;2-3"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_43_3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/(SICI)1521-3773(19990301)38:5<659::AID-ANIE659>3.0.CO;2-P"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_44_2","unstructured":"Racemic1was prepared by the lithiation of 2\u2010alkynyl\u20105\u2010bromopyrimidine followed by treatment with 2\u2010methylpropanal."},{"key":"e_1_2_3_45_2","unstructured":"Preparation of (S)\u20101with ca. 0.00005\u2009%ee. Pyrimidyl alkanol (S)\u20101(1.5 mg >99.5\u2009%ee) was dissolved in ethyl acetate (or benzene) to make a standardized solution of (S)\u20101(3.2\u00d710\u22126mol\u2009L\u22121). The solution (50 \u03bcL) was added to a solution of racemic1(75.1 mg) in ethyl acetate (or benzene). Then a part of the solution was transferred to another flask and the removal of solvent gave (S)\u20101with ca. 0.00005\u2009%ee(9.9 mg). Dissolution of the whole (S)\u20101in 4.3 mL of cumene produced a 9.9\u00d710\u22123\u2009Msolution of (S)\u20101with ca. 0.00005\u2009%ee."},{"key":"e_1_2_3_46_2","unstructured":"\u00a0"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_47_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/cr00013a004"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_48_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/cr000411y"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_49_2","unstructured":"After our experiments were completed Singleton and Vo reported asymmetric autocatalysis using (R)\u2010(2\u2010methylpyrimidyl)alkanol[5b]with the order of 10\u22125\u2009%ee["},{"key":"e_1_2_3_50_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/ja027129o"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_51_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/1615-4169(200207)344:5<453::AID-ADSC453>3.0.CO;2-U"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_52_2","unstructured":"Autocatalyst1on the order of 10\u22129\u2009%eehas been employed but we have not yet received reproducible results probably because of the effect of some unexpected and unknown chiral factor."},{"key":"e_1_2_3_53_2","unstructured":"The reaction of 2\u2010methylpyrimidine\u20105\u2010carbaldehyde withiPr2Zn without any added chiral substance had been examined in 100 experiments. After repeated asymmetric autocatalysis (2\u2010methylpyrimidyl)alkanol with a chirality level above the detection level formed [K.Soai T.Shibata Y.Kowata Japan Kokai Tokkyo KohoJP 9\u20102681791997]. However the probability of the formation ofSandRenantiomers in toluene was not equal which indicates an unexpected and unknown chiral factor affects the asymmetric induction. Similar observations have been reported by Singleton and Vo.[10a]"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_54_2","unstructured":"\u00a0"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_55_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/ja993128t"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_56_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/(SICI)1521-3757(20000417)112:8<1570::AID-ANGE1570>3.0.CO;2-6"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_56_3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/(SICI)1521-3773(20000417)39:8<1510::AID-ANIE1510>3.0.CO;2-R"},{"key":"e_1_2_3_57_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1021\/ja980815w"}],"container-title":["Angewandte Chemie International Edition"],"original-title":[],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.wiley.com\/onlinelibrary\/tdm\/v1\/articles\/10.1002%2Fanie.200390105","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1002\/anie.200390105","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,17]],"date-time":"2023-10-17T04:06:09Z","timestamp":1697515569000},"score":1,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/10.1002\/anie.200390105"}},"subtitle":[],"short-title":[],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2003,1,20]]},"references-count":64,"journal-issue":{"issue":"3","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2003,1,20]]}},"alternative-id":["10.1002\/anie.200390105"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/anie.200390105","archive":["Portico"],"relation":{},"ISSN"